# SPEAR inference server — deployment configuration.
#
# Copy to the real location and fill it in. The real file lives OUTSIDE the
# Git checkout, because it names one machine:
#
#     ~/spear-runtime/config/server.conf
#
# Resolution, for every value below:
#
#     SPEAR_SERVER_<NAME> in the environment   >   this file   >   nothing
#
# The environment wins so that a one-off run ("serve the other quant once")
# needs no edit. Where "nothing" is not an acceptable answer, serve.sh says
# which value is missing and stops; it does not guess.
#
# The file is sourced by bash. Quote anything containing a space.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- required

# The llama-server binary. Built by install-llamacpp.sh, which derives the
# build location from this same value -- one variable, not two.
SPEAR_SERVER_LLAMA_BIN=/srv/spear-runtime/llama.cpp/build/bin/llama-server

# The GGUF to serve, absolute. For a sharded model name the FIRST shard:
# llama.cpp opens it and finds its siblings beside it under their real names.
SPEAR_SERVER_MODEL=/srv/spear-runtime/models/gguf/Model-Q8_0-00001-of-00004.gguf

# Context window, in tokens. REQUIRED, and deliberately without a default.
#
# It is the one setting whose right value is a property of the machine and of
# nothing else: what the VRAM holds, how long an agentic turn runs. Two
# different numbers were in circulation here -- a running server at 98304 and
# a restart script at 65536 -- and the script would silently have brought the
# server back with a third of its context missing. A number no file states is
# a number nobody chose.
SPEAR_SERVER_CTX=32768

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- optional

# Interface and port. 127.0.0.1 keeps the server off the network: reach it
# through an SSH tunnel rather than by binding a shared host's interface.
SPEAR_SERVER_HOST=127.0.0.1
SPEAR_SERVER_PORT=8080

# Concurrent slots. One slot gives a single session the whole KV cache; more
# slots share it, and they then compete for the same cells.
SPEAR_SERVER_PARALLEL=1

# Layers offloaded to the GPU. 99 means "all that fit".
SPEAR_SERVER_NGL=99

# Generation threads. Unset lets llama.cpp choose for the host it is on,
# which is usually right; set it when sharing a machine.
#SPEAR_SERVER_THREADS=

# MoE experts kept on CPU/RAM. Unset auto-detects from the model filename:
# a mixture-of-experts model offloads its experts, a dense one does not.
# 0 forces everything onto the GPU.
#SPEAR_SERVER_NCPUMOE=

# LoRA adapter served on top of the base model. Unset, or "none", serves the
# base alone.
#SPEAR_SERVER_LORA=

# Where fetch-model.sh puts downloaded weights, and which repository and file
# it fetches. Only the fetch tooling reads these.
SPEAR_SERVER_MODELS_DIR=/srv/spear-runtime/models/gguf
#SPEAR_SERVER_MODEL_REPO=owner/Model-GGUF
#SPEAR_SERVER_MODEL_FILE=Model-Q8_0-00001-of-00004.gguf

# HF_HOME is the Hugging Face client's own variable, not one SPEAR invents.
# On a shared machine, point it somewhere of your own rather than pouring
# tens of gigabytes into an account-wide cache others depend on.
#HF_HOME=/srv/spear-runtime/hf
